<title>USA: Nebraska fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</title>
<headline>Nebraska fed cattle market quiet, no trade - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading on slaughter steers and heifers was very quiet, USDA said. Demand and seller light following weekly movement of 80,500 head. Showlists generally well depleted this week.</p>
<p>Live basis sales - Equivalent 3 percent shrink delivered and FOB, some FOB 4% shrink. Dressed basis delivered ( paid on hot carcass weights).</p>
<p>Slaughter Steers -  No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Slaughter Heifers - No confirmed sales.</p>
<p>Confirmed -None  Last Week - 1,000  Last Year - 4,500</p>
<p>For week - None.  Sm Pd Lst Wk - None.  Sm Pd Lst Yr - None.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8720))</p>
</text>
